      ":question/problem": "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -7 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form ${C}_{i}:={C}_{i}+k{C}_{1},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the right of ${a}_{21}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 7\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}: &={C}_{2}-{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 7\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{3}: &={C}_{3}-9{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -7 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-9{C}_{1}.$"
