      ":question/id": "5b007bca-ff70-5f72-b366-01bf0baa6ac8",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-130614",
      ":question/problem": "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form ${C}_{i}:={C}_{i}+k{C}_{1},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the right of ${a}_{31}=-1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}: &={C}_{2}+{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 3 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{3}: &={C}_{3}+4{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+4{C}_{1}.$"
    }
